            <ArticleTitle>RADS and its variants: asthma by another name.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>79-93</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.iac.2012.10.011</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0889-8561(12)00133-6</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article describes the different clinical variants of irritant-induced asthma, specifically focusing on high-dose irritant-induced asthma and irritant-induced work-exacerbated asthma, as well as reviews known causes, addresses the often adverse medical and socioeconomic outcomes of this complex condition, and considers issues of causation from an occupational and environmental medicine perspective.</AbstractText>
